yes(46,'B','Oxygen and copper do not react with water or steam in this comparison. Hot carbon and zinc react with steam. Bromine reacts reversibly with water to form HBr and HOBr, so copper and bromine cannot be the correct pair.',['https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlehtml/2012/ra/c2ra20073b',R],question='Which of these elements will not react with either water or steam?\n1. Carbon\n2. Oxygen\n3. Copper\n4. Bromine\n5. Zinc',options=['1 and 2','2 and 3','3 and 4','1, 2 and 3','2, 3 and 5'],audit='Restored list and steam wording. Changed C to B because bromine hydrolyses, independently corroborated by RSC bromination paper.')
